# config/usage-warner - opt-in thresholds for the local Claude usage warner
# (bin/fm-usage-warner.sh). Copy this into a local, gitignored
# config/usage-warner and edit. One `<window-id>:<percent>` directive per
# non-empty, non-comment line, split on the LAST colon so a per-model window
# id such as `model:fable` still parses correctly.
#
# <window-id> is exactly the "id" field quota-axi's own --json output already
# uses. <percent> is a whole number from 1 to 100. A configured window id the
# account does not return is silently never compared.
#
# <percent> counts percent LEFT, and a window warns when it drops TO OR BELOW
# it - the same direction bin/fm-seat.sh's threshold and the quota viewer count.
# These directives used to count percent USED and warn on rising past the
# number, so a file written against that older reading now means the opposite;
# every warning names both figures ("8% left (92% used)") so it says so the
# first time it speaks. Prefer the setter to editing this by hand:
#
#   bin/fm-usage-warner.sh threshold five_hour 20
#
# An ABSENT config/usage-warner means the feature is off: `check` stays
# completely silent and `arm` refuses. This file's mere presence is the
# opt-in.
#
# The two account-level windows below exist for every account regardless of
# what per-model windows a given account happens to return.
five_hour:20
seven_day:10
